s  um as really the eu just following  through  on what they said but also as not  unusual  for the eu either i think  there was always a degree in terms of  this internal market bill  of this playing into the trade  negotiations boris johnson said even in  a newspaper article  that actually not voting for the  internal market bill would make it  harder  to get a good trade deal so i think we  can't remove what was going on with that  from the context  of trying to get that future  relationship and i i  think this action from the eu this  infringement proceedings from the eu  will probably be viewed by those in  westminster as  part of the sort of rough and tumble tit  for tat  of the trade negotiations and don't  forget as adam was saying these  proceedings can take  a very long time to come to fruition to  get a definite  result and it may well be that we have  reached a point where  a deal is done or a deal is not done  before we actually find out  any eventual result of these proceedings  so at the moment  i think it will probably be shrugged off  here in westminster albeit  expect to see the opposition expect to  see labour the lib dems the smpcs on  this  as evidence of the uk government acting  beyond  international law and acting as they see  it in an irresponsible way
 

